                        Oxfordshire, University</orgName><p>This attribution was first listed (with
                        a query) in the Medieval Libraries of Great Britain Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card (in Neil Ker's
                        handwriting) recorded the following information: <q>Perhaps the presentation
                           copy to Duke Humphrey in 1440. Secundo folio <q>operis incitacio</q>. Cf.
                           list of 1444, no. 133, ed. Sammut, p. 84</q>. However, this suggestion
                        was later rejected in MLGB3 (2010-2015), specifically in the library
                        headnote for Oxford University: <q>BAV, Vat. lat. 10669, tentatively
                           included in the 1987 Supplement as a match for UO3.133 must also be
                           rejected: see M. Zaggia, Interpres (1993).</q>
                     </p></provenance>
